# Client build-time configuration (tech-06 §4.2). Copy to app/.env and fill in.
#
# Expo CLI loads .env from THIS directory only — it does not walk up to the repo root, so
# infra/.env is unrelated to this file and shares nothing with it.
#
# ↯ Baked into the APK at build time. Changing it is prebuild + rebuild + reinstall, never a
# restart (tech-04 §3.2).

# The whole client surface: one URL, including the /api/v1 prefix, no trailing slash.
#
# Use the tailnet HTTPS URL for BOTH dev and release builds — tech-06 §4.2's recommendation.
# The phone is on the tailnet anyway, so it works at home, and it means the configuration you
# develop against is the configuration that ships.
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://<host>.<tailnet>.ts.net/api/v1
#
# The LAN form (http://<pc-lan-ip>:8080/api/v1) is a documented fallback for isolating whether a
# failure is Tailscale's or the API's — needing it is a signal, not a setup step. ↯ It also will
# not work as-is: Android 9+ blocks cleartext HTTP by default, so the LAN form additionally
# requires a usesCleartextTraffic exemption, which is exactly the hole tech-06 §1.2 closed. Do not
# add that exemption casually to make a first request succeed.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# Sentry (tech-06 §9.1) — the `traverser-app` project's DSN, NOT `traverser-api`'s. Separate
# projects so a client crash and a server exception never share a triage queue.
#
# Unlike the URL above this is optional: blank disables capture, so the app builds and runs without
# a Sentry account. A DSN is a public identifier by design — it ships inside the APK and is not a
# secret — but this file stays gitignored anyway.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# development | production. Keeps local experiments out of real issues.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
